  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, and it passes the typecheck. I couldn't run or render it, so colors, lighting and frame rate are untested.\n\n- **Sky and sun:** a custom sky dome shader draws a vertical gradient from orange at the horizon through pink and violet to indigo. It also draws a large low sun with a halo.\n- **Islands:** 11 islands from radius 4 to 24, each with:\n  - a faceted inverted-cone rock underside with lumps;\n  - a grass cap and soil layer;\n  - trees, blossom trees and glowing crystals.\n  They bob at different speeds, amplitudes and phases, and the smaller ones tilt slightly.\n- **Waterfall:** a faded translucent column plus 90 streaming droplets fall from the rim of the largest island. Both follow its bobbing.\n- **Clouds:** 14 soft banks at different depths and heights drift at different speeds. Distant banks are tinted paler, and each fades out and wraps at the edge of the view.\n- **Haze:** exponential lavender-blue fog makes far islands paler and bluer.\n- **Camera:** it swings ±28° around the scene and bobs gently, on a 50-second sine loop, with no user input. It is driven each frame through `app.camera?.setPose`. If `app.camera` is undefined at runtime, the camera stays still.\n- **Contract:** the app draws into `#app` and sets `window.__EVAL_READY__` after the first frames.\n\nThe scene has roughly 250 nodes.\n\n",
